; FileCheck spec for main_trivial.logos.
;
; Asserts an arithmetic-only program lowers to exactly one DEFINED function
; (main) with no monomorphised/stdlib code emitted — i.e. no `define` for any
; `Type__method` or `__g__` specialization. Under the default-on implicit
; prelude every program imports the stdlib surface, which appears as unused
; `declare`s (extern, no body — harmless: gc-sections drops them at link).
; The canary therefore checks for leaked DEFINITIONS (real code bloat), not
; declarations. (Follow-up: prune unreferenced forward-declares once the
; externally-referenced tag-dispatch init fns are retained — plain SymbolDCE
; over-prunes them.)

; CHECK-LABEL: define {{.*}}i32 @main()
; B-ex-01: integer + lowers to llvm.sadd.with.overflow + trap on overflow.
; CHECK: call {{.*}} @llvm.sadd.with.overflow.i64
; CHECK: trunc i64
; CHECK: ret i32

; No monomorphised specialization or stdlib method is DEFINED (declares are OK).
; CHECK-NOT: define {{.*}}__g__
; CHECK-NOT: define {{.*}} @{{[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*}}__
